<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal sets date for third mobile phone operator.</title>
<headline>Portugal sets date for third mobile phone operator.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Candidates for Portugal's third mobile phone licence must present bids by September 15 and a decision will be taken by the end of the year, an Economy Ministry spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>The spokesman said bids must be presented to the country's Communications Institute.</p>
<p>TMN, a subsidiary of Portugal Telecom, and Telecel are the two operators currently in the market.</p>
<p>A number of consortiums have been mentioned in news reports are preparing bids for the third licence. Amongst them are Banco Finantia, the Sonae group, in alliance with Britain's Cable &amp; Wireless Plc, EDP-Electricidade de Portugal and the Maxitel group.</p>
<p>--Jose Barata, Lisbon bureau 3151-3113121</p>
</text>
